# Translations are generated wholesale by the translation workflow, and merging
# them line by line does not work: git happily interleaves two full rewrites of
# the same catalogue and produces duplicate msgid entries, which msgfmt then
# refuses for the whole file. That happened four times, each one silently
# breaking all 28 languages until someone tried to compile them.
#
# Marking them binary makes git refuse the automatic merge and report a
# conflict instead. Failing loudly is the point: the fix is always to take one
# side whole -- normally the workflow's, which regenerates from the current
# source -- never to blend them.
locale/*.po binary
locale/*.pot binary

# Compiled catalogues are build output; there is nothing to merge in them.
usr/share/locale/**/*.mo binary
